  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-06">A shared, direction-symmetric `IThreadResolver` find-or-creates the thread and returns `sprk_thread`, invoked by both inbound capture and outbound send, for all channels. Email = `sprk_inreplyto` ancestry (reply-chain root → thread); chat = ACS `ChatThreadId`. Extends `ThreadContinuityRung` (inbound) + `CommunicationService` (outbound).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project-CRITICAL">This EDITS shared `Services/Communication/` code email-r4 shipped. Author/run characterization tests pinning the CURRENT email inbound matching + outbound send behavior and confirm GREEN BEFORE extending; keep GREEN after. No historical backfill (point-forward).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-024">Thread anchor reuses the polymorphic regarding family — MUST NOT add a second regarding mechanism. The thread record's anchor is the ADR-024 regarding, not a new pointer.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-045">Direction-symmetric per rule 3 — the resolver is invoked from both directions, mirroring the enrichment pattern. Register via the channel-agnostic seam; email + chat resolve their own thread key.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-02">Thread assignment is best-effort and non-fatal — a resolve/create failure MUST NOT fail the send or inbound-capture path (log + continue, message still persists without `sprk_thread`).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Register `IThreadResolver` + its channel strategies via `CommunicationModule` only; DI unconditional (ADR-032 Null-Object if any part is feature-gated).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Integration-heavy; characterization tests for the frozen path FIRST; vertical-slice seam test for the resolver. No `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;` / DI-registration / ctor-null-check tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">`parallel-safe: false` — this task serializes the W4 shared-path edit; 041/042/043 start only after it lands. Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (shared `Services/Communication/`; `notification-spine-r1` also touches this area — align the `threadId` contract at joint intake, not an R1 blocker).</constraint>
    <constraint source="root-§10">bff-extensions Placement Justification in the PR; publish-size delta vs ~45.30 MB baseline; no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>

