    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Direction-symmetric invocation" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationService.cs">
        Enrichment is already invoked from both inbound and outbound (ADR-045 rule 3). Mirror that shape for the thread resolver: one inbound call site (`ThreadContinuityRung`), one outbound (send path), one channel-agnostic seam.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Ancestry reuse (no new matching)" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Engine/ThreadContinuityRung.cs">
        The rung already walks `sprk_inreplyto` ancestry to inherit regarding. Reuse that computed ancestry to resolve the thread (root → thread); do not add a second walk.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Type-keyed strategy" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Channels/CommunicationChannelDispatcher.cs">
        Mirror the dispatcher's `CommunicationType`-keyed resolution for the per-channel thread-key strategy (email = ancestry root; Message = ACS `ChatThreadId`).
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
