  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read `IncomingCommunicationProcessor.cs`, `Engine/ThreadContinuityRung.cs` (regarding-ancestry walk), and `CommunicationService.cs` (send path) to map the exact inbound + outbound call sites and the ancestry data already computed. Read task 004's `sprk_communicationthread`/`sprk_thread`/thread↔channel schema.</step>
    <step order="2">Read `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` §F + root §11 Component Justification + ADR-045 rule 3 + ADR-024 before defining the seam.</step>
    <step order="3">**CHARACTERIZATION FIRST (shared-code safety gate).** Author/confirm characterization tests that pin CURRENT behavior of: (a) existing email inbound matching (regarding inheritance via ThreadContinuityRung ancestry) and (b) the existing outbound send flow. Run them; confirm GREEN. Do NOT edit shared code until these are green. Record the baseline in `current-task.md`.</step>
    <step order="4">Define `IThreadResolver` in `Services/Communication/` — a direction-symmetric `find-or-create` returning `sprk_thread` for a given normalized message + direction, with a per-channel thread-key strategy (email: `sprk_inreplyto` ancestry root; `Message`: ACS `ChatThreadId`). Keep it channel-agnostic at the seam; channel-specific key extraction behind a small keyed strategy.</step>
    <step order="5">Implement the resolver: look up an existing `sprk_communicationthread` by the channel thread-key (ancestry-root id for email; ACS `ChatThreadId` for chat via the thread↔channel child table); create one (thin: topic from first-message subject/participant label, anchor = ADR-024 regarding of the message, default privacy state) when none exists; write/ensure the thread↔channel ref row for chat.</step>
    <step order="6">Extend `ThreadContinuityRung` (inbound): after it computes ancestry/regarding, call the resolver to ALSO set `sprk_thread` (join parent's thread or create). Preserve the existing regarding inheritance exactly.</step>
    <step order="7">Extend `CommunicationService` (outbound send): call the resolver so a reply joins the replied-to message's thread and a fresh message/email creates a thread. One added call; email behavior otherwise unchanged.</step>
    <step order="8">Make both call sites best-effort/non-fatal (NFR-02): wrap the resolve so a failure logs and continues — the message still persists (without `sprk_thread`) rather than failing send/capture.</step>
    <step order="9">Register `IThreadResolver` + channel strategies in `CommunicationModule` (ADR-010), unconditional.</step>
    <step order="9.05">Write the extension tests: an email reply joins its parent's thread; a fresh outbound email creates a thread; a chat message joins its ACS thread; a fresh chat message creates a thread; a resolver failure does NOT fail the persist path (NFR-02). RE-RUN the Step-3 characterization tests — confirm STILL GREEN (existing email flows unchanged).</step>
    <step order="9.1">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` then `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o c:/tmp/msg-040-publish/`; report compressed size + delta vs ~45.30 MB baseline. Expected ≈ 0 (no new package).</step>
    <step order="9.2">Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` — confirm no new HIGH-severity CVE.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor quality gates (REQUIRED — shared-path edit): `code-review` on the diff (focus: frozen email behavior preserved, NFR-02 non-fatal, ADR-024 no second mechanism, §11 justification); `adr-check` against `spec.md`. Address Critical findings; cite bff-extensions Placement Justification. Per root §6.5, surface any ADR tension rather than silently complying.</step>
    <step order="9.6">Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (shared `Services/Communication/` hot-path; coordinate with `notification-spine-r1` on the `threadId` contract — not an R1 blocker).</step>
    <step order="10">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (040 ✅) + reset `current-task.md`; record decisions (seam shape, per-channel key strategy, characterization-test locations, non-fatal wiring).</step>
  </steps>

